<title>USA: Great Western declines to comment on report.</title>
<headline>Great Western declines to comment on report.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-10-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>California-based Great Western Financial Corp declined to comment on a report in Business Week about a rumor that it is being pursued for a friendly merger by an out-of-state commercial bank.</p>
<p>&quot;We never comment on rumors or speculation concerning mergers and acquisitions,&quot; a spokesman for Great Western said.</p>
<p>The magazine quoted an unnamed investment banker as saying a large money-center bank &quot;will approach - if it hasn't done so already - its (Great Western's) management for a friendly merger deal.&quot;</p>
<p>The investment banker said the buyer will have to pay 35 to 37 a share, the publication said.</p>
<p>Great Western closed off 1/8 at 27-1/8.</p>
</text>
